{
  "about": "The UTF-8 byte length of a String, the derived selector {utf8_bytes: <parent>} (docs/design/expression-family-source22.md, \"String .utf8_bytes\" and final review decisions 11 and 19). A `texts` row is one text written as its UTF-16 code units, so a lone surrogate can be written at all: `bytes` is the length of its UTF-8 encoding and `count` its number of Unicode scalar values, both null where the text holds a lone surrogate and is no Unicode text: its byte length is Unknown in every lane, and its `.count` is not asserted here. Each lane binds {label: <text>} and evaluates {compare: {left: {utf8_bytes: label}, op: eq, right: <bytes>}} and {label.count: {eq: <count>}}, and holds its faulty variants (scalar count, UTF-16 units, code points, graphemes) to disagree with at least one row. `evaluate` rows are whole predicates over a row; `refused` rows are documents every reader refuses. Answered by tests/utf8_bytes.rs, the Go fixture ess-conformance/tests/fixtures/utf8-bytes.go and ess-conformance/src/ts/predicate.test.ts.",
